== 3. Verdict ================================================== 
  RASSF9: associated with 1 measure(s): 
    - A1 tumour site (primary vs metastatic) (p.adj = 0.006) 
  RASSF10: associated with 2 measure(s): 
    - A1 tumour site (primary vs metastatic) (p.adj = 9.54e-05) 
    - A4 overall survival (Cox, per log2 unit) (p.adj = 0.015) 

  Reminder: tumour site is NOT a clean aggressiveness measure -- a  
  metastatic sample indicates the disease metastasised, but the  
  expression difference may reflect the tissue the lesion sits in  
  rather than tumour behaviour. Stage, Breslow and survival are the  
  measures that bear on aggressiveness directly. 

